# Keep the shared science log current

This repo is half of a two-tool workflow. Science discussions happen in **Claude
Desktop** (on the Mac); implementation happens here via **Cursor / Claude Code** on
NERSC. The two sides cannot read each other's chats — the *only* shared channel is
`SCIENCE_LOG.md`. A decision or result becomes shared knowledge only if it lands
there, so treat updating it as part of finishing a task, not an optional extra.

`SCIENCE_LOG.md` is at the **root of this (Illustris) repo**.

When you make a **meaningful** change — code, a workflow, a decision, or a result
worth remembering — append a dated entry to the **top** of the
`## Log (newest first)` section, tagged `[code]`:

    ### YYYY-MM-DD — [code] short title
    - What: ...
    - Why / decision: ...
    - Next: ...
    - Refs: files / commits

Guidance: keep it terse; add, never rewrite earlier entries; if you're unsure the
log is current, `git pull` first. After updating, remind the user to commit & push
the log. Skip it only for genuinely trivial, no-op, or read-only work — when in
doubt, log one line.
